# OCR engine — COMMITTED 2026-08-22. Both blockers named in db452ef are cleared:
# the payload was ruled acceptable by Fauzan (TODO.md, "5.01 MB OCR: acceptable
# — 0 KB for the ~98% who never ask"), and the live CSP now carries
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (grant 4567704, confirmed an ancestor of origin/main AND
# read off the production response header). The note that used to sit here
# outlived both conditions by ~3 weeks while sessions kept re-quoting it.
# MEASURED 5.01 MB (tesseract.min.js 0.06 + worker.min.js 0.12 +
# tesseract-core-simd-lstm.wasm.js 3.76 + ind.traineddata 1.07), off the network
# on a real run. Apache-2.0 throughout. Re-fetch: scripts/fetch-ocr-engine.sh.

# Rolling median of recent GREEN gate durations, used to flag a run that was
# starved by machine contention. MACHINE-LOCAL: a baseline from someone else's
# laptop describes their hardware, not this run. Written after the fingerprint
# watcher stops, so it can never move the tree under a run.
.gate-baseline.json
review-shots/
